# Cause & Effect 10: Software engineering in the age of AI

The speakers argue that coding agents change the value of software engineering without removing programming languages or experienced judgment. Cheap code makes building blocks, system structure, verification, and control of complexity more important. [07:47](https://youtu.be/irmz5X3c7Do?t=467) [30:06](https://youtu.be/irmz5X3c7Do?t=1806) [44:51](https://youtu.be/irmz5X3c7Do?t=2691)

They connect Effect and ZIO's properties needed in running applications to agent-written work, and discuss making quality rules executable through types, linting, and review. [50:14](https://youtu.be/irmz5X3c7Do?t=3014) [52:26](https://youtu.be/irmz5X3c7Do?t=3146) [58:23](https://youtu.be/irmz5X3c7Do?t=3503)
